# Gemma 4 12B instruct, Google's quantization-aware-trained INT4 build
# (google/gemma-4-12B-it-qat-w4a16-ct: compressed-tensors W4A16, Marlin on this GPU; Apache-2.0):
# the ~12B mid point of the speed/quality study (reports/speed_quality/). The bf16 checkpoint
# (22.3 GiB) leaves no room for a KV cache on 24 GiB. Thinking only when asked (off here), no system
# turn injected; unlike the pinned Gemma 4 E4B template, the generation prompt opens the model turn
# with an empty thought channel, so the prefill reads
# `<|turn>model\n<|channel>thought\n<channel|>Answer:`. --language-model-only skips the vision tower;
# --max-num-batched-tokens=1024 and --max-num-seqs=16 as in the other presets;
# --generation-config=vllm ignores the upload's sampling defaults; 0.90 of the GPU.
JEVEMU_VLLM_MODEL=google/gemma-4-12B-it-qat-w4a16-ct
JEVEMU_VLLM_MODEL_REVISION=1d2c2d7f2466070e69d6fb3fd5ce9a7d75f2f6ee
JEVEMU_VLLM_DTYPE=bfloat16
JEVEMU_VLLM_MAX_MODEL_LEN=8192
JEVEMU_VLLM_GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.90
JEVEMU_VLLM_DEFAULT_CHAT_TEMPLATE_KWARGS='{"enable_thinking":false}'
JEVEMU_VLLM_EXTRA_ARGS='--language-model-only --max-num-seqs=16 --max-num-batched-tokens=1024 --generation-config=vllm'
